rule NetVerseAjpa(p: fr.pf.core::Personne, a: fr.pf.core::Personne, mois: Date, echeance: Money, retenue: Money) defeasible {
    effective [@2024-01-01, infinity);
    label fr official "AJPA nette après retenue";
    label en unofficial "AJPA net after deduction";
    when retenue_mensuelle_ajpa(p, mois, retenue) and fr.css.ajpa::ajpa_montant_mois(p, a, mois, echeance);
    then net_verse_ajpa(p, mois, net_apres_retenue(echeance, retenue));
}

@source(fr.pf.core::CSS_L553_2, fr.pf.core::CSS_L553_2_CSS_ED2025_02,
        fr.pf.core::CSS_L553_2_CSS_ED2025_09, fr.pf.core::CSS_L553_2_CSS_ED2025_12,
        fr.pf.core::CSS_L553_2_CSS_ED2026_01, fr.pf.core::CSS_L553_2_CSS_ED2026_04,
        fr.pf.core::CSS_L553_2_CSS_ED2026_06,
        fr.casf.rsa::CASF_L262_46, fr.casf.rsa::CASF_L262_46_ED2025_01,
        fr.casf.rsa::CASF_L262_46_ED2025_06, fr.casf.rsa::CASF_L262_46_ED2026_06)
rule NetSansRetenueAjpa(p: fr.pf.core::Personne, a: fr.pf.core::Personne, dette: Money, base: Money, mois: Date, echeance: Money) defeasible {
    effective [@2024-01-01, infinity);
    label fr official "recouvrement écarté : l'échéance d'AJPA est versée entière";
    label en unofficial "recovery barred: the AJPA echeance is paid in full";
    when dette_recouvrable_ajpa(p, dette) and retenue_effective_ajpa(p, base)
        and fr.css.ajpa::ajpa_montant_mois(p, a, mois, echeance) and not_known(retenue_appliquee_ajpa(p));
    then net_verse_ajpa(p, mois, echeance);
}

// --- BOUNDARIES (silence is a finding; no rules) --------------------------
//
// DSS scale (DSS_PENDING). The monthly-levy amounts and their exact base
// sit in an unpinned decree/DSS instruction (cf. B-PFCORE-DATES-MOIS).
// PF levies arrive computed from the 06 bareme layer
// (prelevement_mensuel); non-PF levies arrive as fund-stated Money
// inputs; no scale percentage literal is hardcoded in this file, and no
// installment x rate product is derived anywhere (PC-R07-39).
//
// Pre-2024 mechanics. RSA L. 262-46 PRE2024 (pinned, 2021-2023) carries
// the same cross-benefit list and L. 553-2 renvoi without the 10 %
// sentence; L. 553-2 itself is pinned only from CSS_ED2024_01. All
// rules start 2024-01-01; the identical pre-2024 paragraphs are
// reserved, not encoded.
//
// RSA 77 EUR floor + recouvrable status (R. 262-92, L. 262-46 al. 12).
// Consumed via the imported indu_recouvrable (rs 05 live: floor,
// notification, limitation, no suspensive appeal — never re-derived).
//
// RSA/AAH limitation (L. 262-45, L. 821-5). Both pinned (2 years,
// fraud exception, no 5-year period). RSA limitation arrives inside
// indu_recouvrable; AAH own-limitation is unencoded
// (B-PV-PRESCRIPTION-SPLIT: only the debt on the echeance's own key
// can be limitation-tested here). No defeaters remain in this file.
//
// RSA tiers-payant, remise, L. 133-4-1 cascade, L. 161-1-5,
// R. 262-92-1 notification. Neighbour-owned procedure, encoded
// upstream of indu_recouvrable. The single-repayment option alone
// conditions RetenueRsaApplication directly (contract (a)).
//
// PA prime d'activité. WIRED (B-PV-PA follow-up 6 closed, FINISH-W2):
// Y = PA section above (RSA pattern, 8 rules). PA-source carries
// onto AF/RSA/AAH/housing WIRED (L. 845-3 al. 3 destination list,
// FINISH-W2 cascade follow-up): pa_indu_reporte_sur_* inputs join
// the Dette rules of those echeances. Remainder reserved
// (B-PV-PA-CARRY): PF→PA carry (titre IV inference, MIRROR),
// AAH/housing→PA carries (L. 821-5-1/L. 823-9 mirror-only),
// PA→AJPA (L. 168-8: no AJPA echeance in this layer),
// L. 845-3 al. 4 tiers-payant and al. 6 L. 133-4-1/livre III
// destinations (decree modalities unpinned / outside surveyed
// benefits). Quarterly served echeance (B-PV-PA-TRIMESTRE); no
// CRDS net (B-PV-PA-CRDS); payment-stage rounding silence
// (B-PV-PA-ARRONDI).
//
// AAH/housing 10 % indemnity and own-recovery permissions
// (L. 821-5-1, L. 823-9). Mirror-only; reserved pending pinning.
// PA left this paragraph: L. 845-3 is pinned in the neighbour and its
// 10 % indemnity arrives via indemnite_fraude (Y = PA section). The
// scale math for AAH/housing retenues stays pinned-grounded via the
// L. 553-2 al. 3 scope sentence (see per-family comments).
//
// Housing limitation. SILENCE in the current CCH: no defeater exists
// or can exist for retenue_appliquee_logement. If a future text bars
// housing recovery, add the defeater then.
//
// Repeat-fraud doubling. WIRED (PC-R07-38): every family has a
// strict RetenueReiteration* rule (x2.00) driven by the imported PF
// 07 repeat status or a stated per-family 5-year repeat fact
// (RSA/AAH/housing/PA/AJPA). The uplift itself is always the fixed
// 50 % (x1.50) of D. 553-5, never a stated fraction.
//
// NO-LEDGER. No month-to-month debt exhaustion, no allocation of one
// indu across several same-month echeances beyond the fund's stated
// split, no simultaneous multi-head deduction (contract (d):
// single-head-per-case), no cross-identity join (see IDENTITY in
// the header). The 06 bareme layer carries the ordered-debt ledger
// (D. 553-4 oldest-first allocation); this layer applies the single
// monthly levy to one echeance.
//
// AJPA. WIRED as a destination head (PC-R07-36, Y = AJPA section):
// PF/RSA carries onto future AJPA echeances (L. 553-2 al. 1 list via
// L. 168-8; L. 262-46 list), stated monthly levy, fixed 50 %/x2
// uplift from a stated carried-debt fraud status. AJPA-own recovery
// (L. 168-13/14) stays owned by fr.css.ajpa. Remainder reserved:
// PA→AJPA (L. 845-3 destination list does not name AJPA — SILENCE,
// no input), AAH/housing→AJPA (mirror-only permissions).
//
// Tiers-payant indu (L. 553-2, "par dérogation" sentence). An indu
// on a tiers-payant benefit is recovered from other directly-paid
// benefits under decree modalities; the decree is unpinned and no
// tiers-payant flag exists in this layer. SILENCE, noted.
//
// Subsidised loans (L. 553-2 "prêts" sentence). Same recovery rules
// apply to unreimbursed fund loans; no loan head exists in this
// layer. SILENCE, noted.
//
// Remission for hardship (L. 553-2 "créance réduite ou remise").
// Organ power except on fraud/false declaration; no hardship or
// remission head exists here. SILENCE, noted.
//
// Final-paragraph overflow (L. 553-2, cash benefits of L. 133-4-1
// bodies; titles IV/V of book III; title I of book VIII). Manager
// agreement + no prior indu on those benefits + decree modalities;
// outside the surveyed benefits. SILENCE, noted.
